Subject: [PATCH 4/4] =?UTF-8?q?feat(chat):=20"Event=20API"=20chip=20to=20c?=
 =?UTF-8?q?reate=20a=20"d=C3=A8s=20que"=20automation=20from=20the=20chat?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20home?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- New chip next to "+ Custom" opens a dialog with two fields: "Dès que…"
  (the condition) and "Alors…" (what the pipe does). It writes a new pipe
  ~/.screenpipe/pipes/event-api-<slug>/pipe.md (manual schedule, the
  condition in trigger.custom as a JSON-quoted YAML scalar, the action as
  the prompt), then asks the local Dès que engine to sync.
- The dialog then shows the engine state for that pipe (reusing the
  trigger picker's DesQueEtat): waiting for translation, to validate with
  access and test counts, Valider / Refuser. Nothing runs before Valider.
- A failed write is reported and nothing is claimed as created.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
